{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvSGVsbCUyMElzJTIwZm9yJTIwSGVyb2VzJTIwJTI4MTk2MiUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Hell Is for Heroes","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/nZ0h8V0jsS5NLKdUZIZ2I2xMWtR.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/m1NdU25axOn22J42c9SDt3VNDhf.jpg","description":"World War II drama where the action centers around a single maneuver by a squad of GIs in retaliation against the force of the German Siegfried line. Reese joins a group of weary GIs unexpectedly ordered back into the line when on their way to a rest area. While most of the men withdraw from their positions facing a German pillbox at the far side of a mine-field, half a dozen men are left to protect a wide front. By various ruses, they manage to convince the Germans that a large force is still holding the position. Then Reese leads two of the men in an unauthorized and unsuccessful attack on the pillbox, in which the other two are killed; and when the main platoon returns, he is threatened with court-martial. Rather that face the disgrace, and in an attempt to show he was right, he makes a one-man attack on the pillbox.\n\nRated NR · Released 26 Jun 1962 · United States of America · Language: English · 90 min\nStudio: Paramount Pictures\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"1962","genres":["War","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.5","runtime":"90 min","cast":["Steve McQueen","Bobby Darin","Fess Parker","Harry Guardino","James Coburn","Mike Kellin","Joseph Hoover","Bill Mullikin"],"director":["Don Siegel"],"released":"1962-06-26T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"This is the living hell for heroes","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Don Siegel","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/wjhr8oJr3fVfOphN7lIlr0R6nF9.jpg"},{"name":"Steve McQueen","character":"Pvt. John Reese","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/xUxg7SAM17eEc0rF90gz59Ap0w1.jpg"},{"name":"Bobby Darin","character":"Pvt. Dave 'J.J.'